This license covers the software it accompanies (the "Software"): the mloda
enterprise packages (the code under mloda/enterprise/ of mloda-registry and the
wheels built from it) and the binary wheels the Licensor publishes for them.
The Software is source-available. It is not open source.

Three things are called a license here. This text is the license. A license
key is the signed file some plugins verify before they run. A license agreement
is the written contract for production use.

PERMITTED WITHOUT A LICENSE AGREEMENT

You may:
- view, read, copy and modify the Software for development, testing and
  evaluation;
- install it from PyPI, run its test suites and run automated security scans
  on it;
- build and test your own code against it, including with the documented test
  hooks and the simulated binary of mloda-testing, which are not license key
  functionality;
- keep and pass on unmodified copies as part of a fork, clone or mirror of the
  mloda-registry repository or of a package index, with the notices kept.

PRODUCTION USE REQUIRES A LICENSE AGREEMENT

Production use means operating the Software for your business, for example
processing live data with it or delivering a product or service with it. A
time-limited evaluation to decide on a license agreement is not production use.
Production use requires a license agreement with the Licensor:
https://mloda.ai/enterprise. A plugin gated by a license key runs only with a
key the Licensor issues, for an evaluation or under an agreement, and stops
after the key's grace window. For a plugin without a key, the right to
production use ends with the agreement.

